      "Language": "por",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This essay reflects the contributions of phenomenological studies to nursing care, as exemplified in the knowledge concerning the adhesion of persons suffering from coronary diseases to daily idle talk. It considers that the understanding of human manifestations allows one to interpret attitudes and behaviors and that the contributions of phenomenological studies can facilitate the reach of excellence in nursing care."},
